00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:05.680
WESTON HUTCHINS: Hi.

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:08.230
My name is Weston Hutchins,
and I'm a Product Manager

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:09.850
for GKE On-Prem.

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:11.680
Even with more
and more workloads

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:14.650
moving to the public
cloud, On-Prem software

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:18.490
remains a necessity for many
enterprise organizations.

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:20.230
Every enterprise
has apps that are

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:23.020
difficult to move to the
cloud or restrictions

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:25.720
on where sensitive
workloads can run.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:28.150
Many are looking for
a true hybrid story--

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:30.280
one where they can modernize
the apps for the cloud

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:33.910
but continue running in
their own data center.

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:35.650
Many companies have
looked to Kubernetes

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:37.990
to give them a consistent
environment between on-prem

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:39.550
and cloud.

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:42.410
But getting started with
Kubernetes is challenging.

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:44.310
There are over 50 distributions.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.660
And choosing the right
tools to install Kubernetes

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:48.162
can prove daunting.

00:00:48.162 --> 00:00:50.120
And then once you get a
cluster up and running,

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:52.630
you enter the land
of Day 2 operations

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:54.460
where you not only
need tooling, but

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:57.340
considerable operational
expertise to manage the life

00:00:57.340 --> 00:00:59.890
cycle of a Kubernetes cluster.

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:01.960
We find a lot of
customers that start down

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:04.090
the route of building
their own in-house DIY

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:07.180
tooling to manage Kubernetes
later struggle to keep

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:09.460
that tooling up to date.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:12.210
Google's answer for hybrid
is Cloud Services Platform,

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:15.340
a stack that takes the best of
cloud-native open technologies

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:17.590
like Kubernetes and Istio,
and lets you run them

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:19.250
in your data center.

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:22.180
But the key benefit of CSP
is the collection of cloud

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:25.000
services that integrate your
on-preming cloud workloads

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.610
into a single
unified experience--

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:30.370
services like binary
authorization for security,

00:01:30.370 --> 00:01:32.860
unified login and monitoring
through Stackdriver,

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:34.360
or our centralized
policy management

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.930
that syncs access controls
across all of your clusters.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:40.720
At Next '19, we'll deep
dive into the infrastructure

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:43.670
layer for CSP, GKE On-Prem.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:47.210
GKE On-Prem takes all of
the technology behind GKE

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:50.440
and installs it on top of
VMware in your data center.

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:52.810
Once installed, you
register your cluster

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:55.570
with Google's Cloud Console
to give your administrators

00:01:55.570 --> 00:01:57.970
and developers a single
pane of glass for managing

00:01:57.970 --> 00:01:59.660
their clusters and apps.

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:02.170
In our talk at Next,
we'll take a detailed look

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:04.160
into a real-world use case.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:06.670
Arctiq, one of our CSP
solution providers,

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:09.419
recently rolled out GKE On-Prem
to one of their customers--

00:02:09.419 --> 00:02:12.940
Optiva, a telecommunications
services company.

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:14.710
We'll walk through
Optiva's architecture,

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:17.440
show how GKE On-Prem integrated
with their existing tools

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:20.710
and workflows, and give some
tips for your own installation

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:22.000
of GKE On-Prem.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.460
Check out the breakout session
online, and we'll get you up

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:26.260
and running with GKE
On-Prem in no time.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:29.910
[MUSIC PLAYING]

